# Proposed features recognized from through_chamfer.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F3: outer profile under top cap F8: vertical wall loop F3 F5 F6 F4, top at z=12.0, base at z=0.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F3_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
feature F3_Profile ProfileBoss(z=12.0, extent=12.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 40.0
    60.0 40.0
    60.0 0.0
)

# F7: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; far mouth bevel F2 (1.0 deep at 90.0deg included) opens through -- the other setup's chamfer; a drillable through hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F7_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=12.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Hole, stepover=...)
# the far mouth's 1.0mm bevel at 90.0deg included is the OTHER setup's chamfer: import that setup (--up z-), where it
# is this hole's chamfer_depth, and give this hole there (given from <this project> up=z-)
feature F7_Hole CylinderBore(dia=12.0, extent=12.0, x=20.0, y=20.0)

# F8: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F8_Top Plane(z=12.0)

# F9: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F10 -- a milled bore (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F9_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
feature F9_Bore CylinderBore(dia=8.0, extent=7.0, x=45.0, y=20.0)
